31:       {name:'Oaxaca, Mexico',short:'Oaxaca',emoji:'🌞',tag:'MOUNTAIN TOWN · MEXICO',palette:['#f4d293','#6b9b81','#c76843','#e9b46b'],clues:['Zapotec and Mixtec are among the Indigenous languages spoken here, alongside Spanish.','Oaxaca City sits in a valley framed by the Sierra Madre del Sur.','The region is known for many distinct moles—not just one recipe.'],fact:'Oaxaca is home to many Indigenous communities and languages. Its foodways and traditions vary from town to town.',contrast:'Compare: Yucatán is a low-lying peninsula with a strong Maya-language presence; Oaxaca is a mountainous, highly multilingual region.'},
32:       {name:'Kerala, India',short:'Kerala',emoji:'🌴',tag:'BACKWATER COUNTRY · INDIA',palette:['#e8c879','#5b9e84','#337f70','#f0a477'],clues:['Malayalam is the state’s main official language.','A network of lagoons and canals is known as the backwaters.','Onam is celebrated by many communities; pookalam flower designs are one festive tradition.'],fact:'Kerala has Hindu, Muslim, Christian, Jewish and other communities, with lively regional and local differences.',contrast:'Compare: Goa lies farther north on India’s west coast, with Konkani among its major languages; Kerala’s main language is Malayalam.'},
